# What stays out of version control: everything personal (paths, login, calibration choices),
# everything the bot regenerates, and third-party PR data. See README.md, "O que é seu e o que é
# do bot". Versioned: bin/, lib/, schemas/, README.md, .editorconfig, .gitignore.

# Runtime cache and data: disposable, recreated on every run.
# runs/ logs · cache/ diff, meta, triage per PR · worktrees/ checkouts · state/ locks
/.bugbot/

# Retro: permanent record of review decisions per PR, read by `bugbot retro`.
# Not cache (purge only deletes it with --retro), but personal: it holds third-party PR data.
/retro/

# Eval set (reserved): curated PRs with confirmed bugs; third-party code, never shared here.
/evals/

# Personal configuration written by `bugbot setup`: clone paths and the gh login of whoever runs it.
/workspace.json

# Per-repository review rules: created by `bugbot setup`, calibrated by each reviewer.
/repos/

# Settings written by `bugbot init` (defaults from schemas/settings.schema.json x-init) and
# personal overrides on top of them.
/bugbot.json
/bugbot.local.json

# Atomic writes: temporary files renamed over the target; left behind only if a run is killed.
.workspace.*.json
.bugbot.json.*
*.tmp
*.format-tmp

# Claude Code: personal settings (.claude/skills is a versioned symlink to .agents/skills)
/.claude/settings.local.json

# Editors, system and Python noise
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
__pycache__/
*.pyc
